  "B_proofcontracts": {
    "ex-unequal-dimensional-proper-pushforwards-have-the-summed-dimension-ext-bm-shift": {
      "statement": "For trivial G, E=pt, X1=pt, X2=P1, d1=0,d2=1, Ext^r(k,R\u0393(P1,k)[1]) is k for r=\u22121,1 and zero otherwise; its BM degrees are 2,0. The reverse corner has the same two Ext degrees.",
      "proof": "Cellular cohomology of P1 has one generator in degrees0,2. R\u0393k[1] has summands k[1],k[\u22121], hence Hom(k,R\u0393k[1+r]) is nonzero exactly r=\u22121,1. Dual Hom gives the reverse degrees. H_BM(P1)=H(P1) is k in degrees2,0. The summed-dimension formula is1\u2212r; using2dim(source)\u2212r would fail one corner.",
      "deps": [
        "thm-proper-pushforward-ext-is-equivariant-borel-moore-homology-of-the-fiber-product"
      ],
      "checked": "Both corners and both nonzero degrees; trivial G illustrates normalization without stabilization."
    },
    "ex-a-point-and-projective-line-check-source-first-convolution-and-opposite-composition": {
      "statement": "In the same point/P1 geometry, \u03b1:k\u2192R\u0393k[1][\u22121] is the unit of degree\u22121, and \u03b2:R\u0393k[1]\u2192k[1] is point evaluation of degree+1. Then \u03b1*\u03b2=\u03b2[\u22121]\u2218\u03b1=id_k, and BM[P1]*[point]=[pt].",
      "proof": "\u03b2[\u22121] is evaluation H0(P1)\u2192k at a point, so it sends constant1 to1; therefore composition of \u03b1 and \u03b2 is identity. \u03a6(\u03b1) is the positive fundamental class in degree2 and \u03a6(\u03b2) is the normalized point class in degree0. Refined diagonal intersection of [P1] and [point] is [point] with positive complex orientation; proper integration to pt gives1. This independently tests the middle drop2, source-first order and lack of an extra shift sign.",
      "deps": [
        "thm-proper-pushforward-ext-is-equivariant-borel-moore-homology-of-the-fiber-product",
        "thm-verdier-duality-identification-intertwines-yoneda-product-and-convolution"
      ],
      "checked": "Nontrivial off-diagonal product returning the point corner; swapped corner is not confused with the P1 identity."
    }
  },
